OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-$-%%%-!-%%%" ,%-$ -$%%-% ,,
OL,3,GNEWSACanterbury's Bayeux Tapestry role
OL,4,Aexplored in play
OL,5,
OL,6,FHistorians believe the embroidery was
OL,7,Flikely to have taken place in
OL,8,FCanterbury and local director and
OL,9,Fauthor Stewart Ross used that as
OL,10,Finspiration for his play The Tapestry.
OL,12,F"It's about the little people, the
OL,13,Fpeople in the margins, not the macho
OL,14,Fmen on horses," said Ross.
